,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"P-3 is finished and passes: the four driver scripts and the bead-map picker are written, and every offline dry/mock run passes. No LabVIEW, camera, motor or serial port was used, nothing is running, and `tasklist` shows 0 LabVIEW processes (12:36). The report is `tools/bench/lean_bench/lean_report_p64p3.md`. The start condition was met (p64prep PASS, p64p1 PASS), and the task text agrees with all of `user_notes.md`, so nothing had to be overridden.\n\n**What each script showed on recorded data:**\n- **`p64_sum.py`** (lost frames from column 0, same formula for both arms): W100 gives **1068**, the observer W100 run 1068, P62 0.\n- **`p64_own.py`** (buffer-number check against the logged start value):\n  - **PASS** on the recorded observer leg: 1474 of 1474 rows match their picks in order, end lag 2.\n  - **FAIL** on a copy with column 0 shifted by +1, and on a copy one ring lap (20 frames) behind.\n  - **NOT RUN** when the wrapper file has 0 lines, 2 lines, 4 lines, or is missing.\n  - In the PASS case the one wrapper line is a stand-in (that replay run had no wrapper); it proves the tool, not a live value.\n- **`p64_leg.py`**: on the recorded W100 leg, 15 picks registered and 15 panels closed. Lost by column 0 is 1068, while the VI's `Total Lost Frames` indicator reads \"0\". The bead-map picks reach the leg without changing `drive_m8.py`.\n- **`p64_abba.py` mock**: refusals (a) LabVIEW present, (b) a planted `getbuff_first.txt` and (c) a stale pick log each stopped the leg with nothing launched. The clean single-leg case and the full A-B-B-A-OBS run were not refused. After an OBS leg the two files are moved into that leg's folder, never deleted.\n- **`p64_abba.py` dry run on the real disk**: the OBS leg would be refused today by (c), because `out_latest2\\picklog_w100.txt` still exists. The checklist's step 7 moves it into its own leg folder; I did not move it.\n\n**One prediction missed.** On a real recorded camera frame the bead finder first found 0 beads, though I had predicted at least 15. A real bead is a flat dark disk inside a bright ring, and my first settings split each bead into several spots. I changed the settings and the clustered-bead test, and the same frame now gives 31 single beads with 15 picked. A frame with only 8 beads left gives 8 bead picks plus 7 fill points in empty field. The settings are tuned on that one frame, so your check of the PNG on the rig day stays the real gate.\n\n**Not done:** checking online whether the TypeSafe/Jev API now accepts images. Web search and fetch were refused by this session's permissions, and I did not try another route. The project files say Jev cannot take images, so option J is a design and cost estimate only, about $0.026 and 3 minutes per snapshot.\n\n**Mistake fixed:** I first wrote guessed times into the report, two code comments and the questions file. I corrected them from the real clock and file times, and the report says so.\n\nThe rig-day checklist is `tools/bench/lean_bench/p64_rigday_checklist.md`. Nothing was committed and no bead or rig-day task was queued.\n\nQuestions for you, also added to `questions_for_user.md`:\n1. **Assumption (fewer than 15 beads):** I fill the missing picks with the earlier ABBA's fixed positions in empty field, so every leg (A, B and OBS) uses the same 15 picks. I report the real bead count N per leg, and a bead that moves between the two snapshots is not picked. Tell me if you want something else.\n2. **Minimum N:** should there be a minimum number of real beads below which the bead run stops, or should it run with fewer than 15 picks? Without an answer I report N and run 15 picks.\n3. **Sample option R, M or J?** I recommend **R** (reference beads, filled to 15).\n   - **R**: it is the sample you are already preparing, needs no new VI build, and its tools are ready.\n   - **M** (magnet kept at 0 mm): needs the panel setting `If no: current pos z?` (normally 30) changed on every leg copy, which is a new build task.\n   - **J** (Jev picks the beads): can be added later to help the bead finder.\n\nRESULT {\"p64p3\": \"PASS\", \"scripts\": 5, \"dry\": \"sum 4/0 (W100 lost 1068), leg 10/0, own 11/0 (recorded PASS, shifted FAIL, one-lap FAIL, 0/2/4/missing lines NOT RUN), abba mock 11/0 + dry 5/0 (today slot O refused by c), beadmap 6/0 (real frame N 31 after one revision)\", \"refusals_tested\": \"a,b,c\", \"minutes\": 19}","ttft_ms":1338,"type":"result","duration_ms":1132186,"uuid":"b6cafcc8-68b8-4c7a-a47d-57d62e555a38","ttft_stream_ms":795,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":795,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
